# After every code change: sync → commit → push

The Windows host runs the code from a VMware shared folder, not from this checkout.
Editing files here changes nothing on Windows until `sync.sh` runs, so a "still broken"
report right after an edit usually means the sync step was skipped.

Run all three steps, in order, once the change is complete:

```bash
cd job-apply-project
./sync.sh                       # rsync to the HGFS share the Windows host reads
git add -A && git commit -m "…" # see identity rules below
git push
```

## Commit identity

Commit as the repo owner only. The configured `user.name` / `user.email` are already
correct — never override them with `--author`, `-c user.*`, or `GIT_AUTHOR_*`.

Never add AI attribution trailers to the commit body:

```
# ❌ BAD
Fix Playwright sync API crash under the FastAPI event loop

Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>

# ✅ GOOD
Fix Playwright sync API crash under the FastAPI event loop
```

No `Co-authored-by`, no "Generated with", no tool name in the message.

## Notes

- `sync.sh` excludes `venv`, `__pycache__`, `node_modules`, the browser profile dirs, and
  `extension/test-forms/captured` (real capture data that `--delete` would otherwise wipe).
- After syncing Python changes, the Windows service needs a `start.bat` restart to pick them up.
